---
import { SITE_NAME, BUSINESS_CONTACT_EMAIL } from "@/lib/site";
---

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
  <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">Legal</p>
  <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-ink">Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-faint">Updated August 2026</p>

  <div class="mt-8 max-w-prose space-y-8">
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What {SITE_NAME} is</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        {SITE_NAME} is a directory that helps consumers find and evaluate local businesses in
        New Jersey, New York, and Pennsylvania. We verify certain facts — like license
        registrations — against official sources at a point in time, and we say when and where
        we checked. We are not a party to any transaction between you and a listed business,
        and we don't guarantee any business's work.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Verification is a snapshot</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        A "license verified" badge means the named registry showed the business in good
        standing on the date shown. Licenses can lapse or be revoked afterward. Registration
        or licensure is not a government endorsement of competency. Always confirm current
        status for significant projects — every badge names the registry so you can.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Reviews and submissions</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Content you submit — reviews, photos, claims — must be truthful, based on your own
        experience, and yours to share. We may decline or remove content that is fake,
        defamatory, or unrelated to a real customer experience. By submitting content you give
        us a non-exclusive license to display it on the site.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Business listings</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Claiming a listing requires that you are authorized to represent the business. Paid
        tiers buy verification work and labeled placement only; they never change rankings or
        reviews, and we may end a paid placement that violates our
        <a href="/editorial-policy" class="font-medium text-brand underline underline-offset-2">editorial policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Paid plans</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Verified ($29/month or $290/year) and Featured ($99/month or $990/year) are recurring
        subscriptions billed through Wix Payments until canceled. Featured placement is limited
        to three businesses per category per county; when slots are full you may join a
        waitlist. Cancellation stops renewal and the plan's benefits end at the close of the
        paid period — Featured placement lapses automatically on its end date. Paid plans buy
        verification work and labeled placement only: they never change organic rankings,
        reviews, or badge outcomes, and a failed license check is not refundable as such —
        the badge simply isn't granted until the registry shows good standing. We may end a
        placement that violates the editorial policy, with a pro-rata refund of the unused
        period.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The site is provided as-is. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} is not
        liable for the acts, omissions, or work quality of any listed business, or for
        decisions you make based on directory content. Nothing here limits rights you have
        under applicable consumer-protection law.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS_CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="font-medium text-brand underline underline-offset-2">{BUSINESS_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
